  "created": "2025-01-31T17:13:28.665Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "While idling in a [world](https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_081568d8-3f1b-493b-bf0c-ecfe81400ae2) for a few hours everyone in the instance slowly started to crash out one-by-one. Checking our system specs we realized our VRAM was slowly filling up, followed by system RAM, followed by pagefile. The world in question had a row of 7 image loaders that would cycle through images on a timer, so my immediate suspicion is that it's not deallocating memory properly. **Turning off \"Allow Untrusted URLs\" causes memory usage to stop climbing**.",
